steps.task:
You are the sole implementation and PR owner for chrisdoc/hevy-mcp. The following are independent read-only triage reports for all currently open issues:

{previous}

Synthesize them against the actual checkout and issue data. Select only a confirmed, reproducible bug or a tightly related small set that can be fixed safely in one focused PR; do not implement feature requests, speculative changes, or already-fixed reports. If reports conflict, verify the relevant code and run a red-capable feedback loop yourself. Follow /root/hevy-mcp/AGENTS.md and the repository AGENTS.md: preserve the fresh branch fix/github-issues-review based on origin/main, use mise, add regression tests before the fix where a correct seam exists, add the required non-empty changeset for runtime-visible package changes, run focused tests plus required checks, and keep secrets redacted. You may modify only this worktree. Once validated, make an atomic Conventional Commit, push fix/github-issues-review, and open a GitHub FIX PR against main using the configured GitHub integration or gh. Do not merge or close issues. If no issue is sufficiently actionable, make no changes and report why. Return the selected issue(s), root cause, changed files, tests and commands, commit, PR URL (or explicit no-PR result), and residual risks.

Act as the synthesis gate for a fix PR. You have five independent read-only diagnoses for the currently open issues in chrisdoc/hevy-mcp below. Inspect the current repository in /root/hevy-mcp-issue-fixes and verify the strongest claims against source and tests before deciding. Select at most one coherent, high-confidence bug family for a single focused PR; related issue numbers may be grouped, but do not combine unrelated fixes. Prefer a reproducible issue with a real regression-test seam. Closed or already-fixed historical work is out of scope here. If the evidence is insufficient or no safe fix is justified, set proceed=false. Do not edit files, commit, push, or change GitHub. Return a concrete implementation plan, not code.

TRIAGE FINDINGS:
{triageFindings}

You are the only mutation-capable implementation worker. Work in /root/hevy-mcp-issue-fixes on branch fix/github-issues-review, which must remain based on origin/main. The synthesis plan and supporting diagnoses are below.

SYNTHESIS PLAN:
{plan}

SUPPORTING DIAGNOSES:
{triageFindings}

If plan.proceed is false, do not edit, commit, push, or create a PR; report that no safe fix was selected. Otherwise implement only the approved focused scope. Read AGENTS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/test-lanes.md, and relevant package/topology guidance before changing code. Follow the diagnosing-bugs discipline: add the regression test at the correct seam before the fix, run it red if possible, implement the smallest fix, run it green, and rerun the original red-capable reproduction. Use the repository's mise-pinned Node/npm commands and keep secrets out of output. Add a non-empty Changeset for every affected shipped package and transitive consumer required by repository/topology.json; use an empty changeset only if the diff truly has no release trigger. Run the narrow relevant lane plus the required PR baseline as practical, including check:changeset. Keep the diff focused and do not modify unrelated existing work. Commit with a Conventional Commit message, push the feature branch, and open a pull request against main using the configured GitHub integration; if that integration is unavailable, use gh as the documented fallback. Do not merge or close issues. Report the changed files, exact validation commands/results, commit SHA, PR URL, and residual risks. Never claim success for a command you did not run.

